module gunbc.predicate_cause_aliasing_roster

// THE CLASS-B REMAINDER, ENUMERATED BY IDENTITY.
//
// v2.std.subject_evidence names two mechanically different violations. Class A -- a coproduct with
// distinct causes folded to one Bool, tell being a discarded payload on a non-pass arm -- was
// enumerated and migrated by its own lane. This roster carries CLASS B: functions returning Bool that
// conjoin host-effect success bits, where nothing is discarded and the predicate's truth set is simply
// wider than the proposition it is cited to prove.
//
// WHY BY MODULE AND SYMBOL AND NOT BY COUNT. A merge-blocking assertion against a number measured on
// the current tree is the oracle DESIGN section 5 forbids: automating its update collapses it to
// measure() == measure(), and the manual update was the whole content. Rows are identities, so a
// migrated site is removed by NAME and the roster can only shrink. The size of this list is prose and
// is deliberately not asserted anywhere.
//
// WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED, AND IT IS THE MOST IMPORTANT SENTENCE HERE. Nothing checks these rows. There is
// no lens reading whether a named symbol still conjoins success bits, so a row that has been migrated
// and not removed, and a site newly authored in this shape, are both invisible. This roster sits at
// MITIGATABLE -- review diligence -- and calling it a wall would be the rung inflation DESIGN section
// 4b names as worse than sitting low.
//
// NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, AND THE SEAM ALREADY EXISTS AND EXECUTES. The declaration index landed for the
// cited-symbol wall inside the parse phase of the required run, deriving one record per module from a
// parse that already happens. A reader over that index that flags a Bool-returning declaration
// conjoining two or more host-effect success reads would make this class mechanically preventable at
// that same seam, from each module's own source, with no corpus walk. This trigger is therefore
// concrete rather than aspirational: what is missing is the reader, not the seam. Until it exists
// these are obligations, not guarantees.
//
// THREE SITES ARE ABSENT FROM THIS LIST ON PURPOSE and are recorded so the absence is not read as
// completeness. tools.self_host_curated_seed_linked_harness cssl_seed_linked_behavioral_receipt was
// migrated by the class-A lane, whose repair replaced a single fault_run.success bit with an exact
// marker observation. tools.emit_host_transport run_rust_smoke and run_python_smoke are migrated in a
// separate change already in review, which lifted their comparison out of the shell transport first.

import std.logic { Bool }
import std.types { String }
import v2.std.algebra { fold_list }
import v2.std.collection { List }

type AliasedPredicateSite {
  module_path: String
  symbol: String
  proposition: String
  aliased_causes: String
}

